OPTION E — Three-zone single row
=================================

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                         │
│  (tree content above)                                   │
│                                                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  [Boost]  [██░░ Claude]  [██░░ Codex]                   │  ← usage
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  [+task]      [agent●3] [panel] [⊟]      [···] [≡] [⚙] │  ← 3 zones
│   primary       runtime state              meta         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

· Left zone = primary action (new task)
· Center zone = runtime indicators (clickable)
· Right zone = meta + view switch + settings
· "···" = workspace toggles (zen/explode/folder), update,
   leaderboard, usage analytics, onboarding, what's new,
   keyboard, feedback
· Settings = last
· Pros:  spatially balanced, intent-driven left→right
         flow (do → observe → configure)
· Cons:  workspace toggles (zen/explode) buried in dropdown
         even though they're frequent
